From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: guard against a NULL IPA model in kbase_get_real_power_locked

Observed on O6N/cixmini across rc4, rc5 and 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next
(serial console capture 2026-07-28): the CIXH5000 (mali) platform
probe calls into kbase_csf_protected_memory_init(), which can return
-EPROBE_DEFER (-517) if the protected_memory_allocator device hasn't
finished its own probe yet. kbase_device_init() correctly unwinds and
returns the error in that case, deferring the whole mali_kbase probe.

But power_control_init() (which runs earlier in the same dev_init[]
table and drives the devfreq/IPA cooling registration) can already
have a kworker in flight by the time protected memory allocator fails
and the probe unwinds. That kworker calls into
kbase_get_real_power_locked() -> get_current_model(), which reads
kbdev->ipa.fallback_model / kbdev->ipa.configured_model -- fields that
are only populated by kbase_ipa_init(), a step later in the sequence
than power_control_init() and one that never got a chance to run
before the probe bailed out. The result is a NULL kbase_ipa_model
pointer, and get_dynamic_coeff() -> model->ops->get_dynamic_coeff
dereferences it, panicking with:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000010
  kbase_get_real_power_locked+0xb0/0x378 [mali_kbase]
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception

This is a probe-vs-async-work teardown race, not something callers
can fully close from outside the IPA code (the devfreq governor's
polling kworker isn't guaranteed to be quiesced before an early
dev_init[] failure unwinds a later-registered subsystem). Guard the
one dereference that actually crashes: if get_current_model() returns
NULL (IPA never initialized, or already torn down), report zero power
for that sample instead of dereferencing a null model. This matches
the existing "GPU powered off" bail-out a few lines above and is a
one-sample-of-zero cost, not a functional regression, on the hardware
path where IPA is actually up.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/ipa/mali_kbase_ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/ipa/mali_kbase_ipa.c
@@ -771,6 +771,17 @@
 
 	model = get_current_model(kbdev);
 
+	if (!model) {
+		/* IPA not initialized yet (or already torn down) -- avoid
+		 * dereferencing model->ops below. See commit message for
+		 * the protected-memory-allocator EPROBE_DEFER race this
+		 * guards against.
+		 */
+		dev_warn_once(kbdev->dev, "kbase_get_real_power_locked: no IPA model, reporting 0 power\n");
+		*power = 0;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	err = model->ops->get_dynamic_coeff(model, power_coeffs);
 
 	if (err && model != kbdev->ipa.fallback_model) {
